# Bicep — style guide

Source: `wiki/Design-Authority/Processes/code-style-and-best-practices-guide/Bicep-style-guide.md` · [Bicep best practices](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-resource-manager/bicep/best-practices) · [AVM](https://azure.github.io/Azure-Verified-Modules/)

Follow [Microsoft Bicep file structure](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-resource-manager/bicep/file) plus these repo rules.

## Generated code readability

- **No double dashes (`--`)** in comments; use `//` above each resource/module block.
- **Comment intent** before each `resource`, `module`, and non-obvious `var`: what it deploys, MCSB control, and parameter dependencies.
- Group related resources with a `// --- Section: ... ---` header (single hyphens only in section headers).

## Naming
Full decision guide: `engineering.mdc`. **Bicep — use this case when:**

| When you write… | Case | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| A **`param`** | **camelCase** | `param storageAccountName string` |
| A **`var`** | **camelCase** | `var diagnosticSettingName = '...'` |
| A **resource/module symbol** (identifier in code) | **camelCase** | `resource storageAccount 'Microsoft.Storage/...'` |
| The **`name:`** property (value Azure stores) | **kebab-case** / CAF | `name: 'mgt-pol-prd-id001'` |
| A **`.bicep` file name** | **kebab-case** | `policy-assignment.bicep` |

**Never in Bicep identifiers:** PascalCase, snake_case, or SCREAMING_SNAKE for `param`/`var`/symbols. Constants → use `param` + `@allowed` or a `var`.

## File order

1. `metadata module` block
2. `targetScope` (if not default resource group)
3. `param` declarations
4. `var` declarations
5. `resource` / `module` / `output`

## Module metadata (required)

Every template starts with:

```bicep
metadata module = {
  version: '1.0.0'
  author: 'ContributorTag'
  name: 'Human-readable module name'
  source: 'https://dev.azure.com/gemeente-den-haag'
  description: 'What this module deploys.'
}
```

Required fields: `version`, `author`, `name`, `source`, `description`.

## Target scope

Declare immediately after metadata when not default RG scope:

`resourceGroup` | `subscription` | `managementGroup` | `tenant`

## Parameters

- Declare after `targetScope` (or after metadata if no targetScope).
- Names: **camelCase**.
- **`@description()` on every parameter.**
- **`@secure()`** on secrets and sensitive values.
- Use `@allowed`, `@minLength`, `@maxLength`, `@minValue`, `@maxValue` where appropriate.
- Decorators directly above the parameter they apply to.
- **Avoid default values** unless there is a clear reason.

## Variables

- Below parameters; **camelCase**; explicit intent.

## Quality gates

- Run **`az bicep build`** and **Bicep linter** before commit (pipeline validation stage required).
- Run **PSRule for Azure** in CI — templates must pass CAF / Well-Architected policy rules aligned with tenant baseline.
- No secrets in parameter files — use `@secure()` params supplied at deploy time / Key Vault refs.
- Align resource naming with Design Authority CAF naming rules (see `architecture.mdc`).

## MCSB & BIO 2.0 defaults (GDH tenant baseline)

GDH MG assigns **Microsoft Cloud Security Benchmark** + **NL BIO Cloud Theme V2**. Per-policy effects aim for maximum **Deny** and **DINE/Modify** without breaking approved patterns; remaining controls stay **Audit**. IaC must still deploy compliant resources or document an **ADR + CISO escalation** for exceptions.

When authoring resources, apply these defaults unless an approved pattern/ADR states otherwise:

- **TLS 1.2+** (`minimumTlsVersion: TLS1_2`) on storage, app, and API endpoints.
- **No anonymous public access** — `allowBlobPublicAccess: false`, `publicNetworkAccess: Disabled` where service supports it.
- **Identity over keys** — MSI for runtime; set `allowSharedKeyAccess: false` when MSI/RBAC path is proven.
- **Private Endpoints** for PaaS where reference architecture / MCSB expects private connectivity.
- **Diagnostic settings** to platform Log Analytics — or record explicit gap in LLTD/backlog.
- **Mandatory tags** per controlled vocabulary before subscription-level inheritance applies.
- Prefer **Azure Verified Modules (AVM)** / approved pattern modules over one-off resource blocks.
- **Policy assignments** at MG scope: manage as Bicep; validate in **Canary Tenant** before production promotion.

## Module & composition patterns

- **Prefer AVM** (`br/public:avm/...`) or approved internal modules over raw `resource` blocks.
- **Module interfaces:** expose only required `params`; use `outputs` for IDs/names downstream modules need.
- **`existing` keyword** for cross-RG/VNet references; do not duplicate data-plane resources.
- **Scope explicitly:** deploy at lowest valid scope (RG > sub > MG); avoid tenant-wide modules unless pattern requires.
- **No hardcoded** subscription/resource IDs in orchestration; pass via parameters from configuration `.jsonc`.
- **Dependency order:** implicit via reference (`resourceId`, module outputs); avoid unnecessary `dependsOn`.
- **Tags:** pass common tag object param; apply to all taggable resources in module.

## Outputs & contracts

- Every module **outputs** resource IDs and names consumers need (PE connection name, MSI principal ID, etc.).
- Document outputs in module `description` metadata and parent pattern README.
- Use `@secure()` on outputs only when value is secret (rare); prefer Key Vault references.

## Enterprise deployment safety

- **`@batchSize(1)`** or sequential deploy for resources with strict ordering (e.g. RBAC after MSI creation).
- **Resource locks** via separate module or policy; document if pattern skips locks (sandbox only).
- **Diagnostic settings** as sibling resource or dedicated sub-module; never optional in production patterns without ADR.
- **Policy compliance:** run PSRule in CI; fix or exempt with documented ADR before merge.
- **What-if** mandatory in production pipeline immediately before deploy stage.

## Anti-patterns (reject in review)

- Copy-paste resource blocks instead of module reuse.
- Inline secrets or connection strings in `properties`.
- `publicNetworkAccess: Enabled` on PaaS without ADR + CISO path.
- Missing `@description` on params (blocks reviewer understanding).
- `allowedValues` too broad on environment param (accidentally deploys wrong env to prod scope).

## bicepconfig.json & linter

- Repo root **`bicepconfig.json`**: enable linter rules aligned with CAF (`core-rules` + org overrides documented in README).
- **`analyzers`** block: treat linter warnings as errors in CI (`bicep build` + exit on warning if pipeline supports).
- **Module aliases** for internal registry paths to shorten `module` references and pin registry.

```jsonc
// bicepconfig.json: central linter and module alias config
{
  "analyzers": {
    "core": {
      "enabled": true,
      "rules": {
        "no-unused-params": "warning",
        "prefer-interpolation": "warning"
      }
    }
  },
  "moduleAliases": {
    "gdh": {
      "registry": "<acr>.azurecr.io"
    }
  }
}
```

## Parameter files (.bicepparam / .jsonc)

- **Secrets never** in `.bicepparam`; use `@secure()` param supplied at deploy time from Key Vault / pipeline secret variable.
- **Environment separation:** one parameter file per environment (`prd-rg001.bicepparam.jsonc`); validate `environment` param matches target scope.
- Comment non-obvious tokens in JSONC; keys **camelCase** per `engineering.mdc`.

```bicep
// pattern-module.bicepparam: environment-specific values only (no secrets)
using '../patterns/storage-account.bicep'

param storageAccountName = 'app-sto-prd-sa001'
param environment = 'prd'
param enablePrivateEndpoint = true
```

## Conditional & incremental deployment

```bicep
// Deploy PE only when private connectivity is required (Profile A3 may set false with ADR)
param enablePrivateEndpoint bool

resource privateEndpoint 'Microsoft.Network/privateEndpoints@2023-04-01' = if (enablePrivateEndpoint) {
  name: '${storageAccountName}-pe001'
  // ...
}
```

- Use **`existing`** for resources owned by another team/RG; do not redeploy hub assets from app patterns.
- **`@batchSize(1)`** on nested deployments when RBAC must follow MSI creation order.

## Diagnostic settings pattern (MCSB LT-3)

```bicep
// Send all supported logs and metrics to central LAW (replace workspace resource ID via param)
param logAnalyticsWorkspaceResourceId string

resource diagnosticSettings 'Microsoft.Insights/diagnosticSettings@2021-05-01-preview' = {
  name: 'send-to-law'
  scope: storageAccount
  properties: {
    workspaceId: logAnalyticsWorkspaceResourceId
    logs: [ { categoryGroup: 'allLogs', enabled: true } ]
    metrics: [ { category: 'AllMetrics', enabled: true } ]
  }
}
```

## Resource locks (production platform)

```bicep
// CanNotDelete lock on production platform RG resources (skip in sandbox)
param applyResourceLock bool = false

resource lock 'Microsoft.Authorization/locks@2020-05-01' = if (applyResourceLock) {
  name: 'canNotDelete'
  scope: storageAccount
  properties: {
    level: 'CanNotDelete'
    notes: 'Platform pattern; remove via IaC only'
  }
}
```

## Policy assignment via Bicep (MCSB / BIO)

- Assign initiatives at **management group** scope with `enforcementMode: Default` on GDH. Set effect parameters per policy (Deny / Audit / DINE / Modify); do not assume a blanket Deny on every MCSB and BIO policy.
- **`nonComplianceMessages`:** user-facing text for Deny (portal deploy, ARM API); keep concise, link to wiki runbook.
- Test **Modify/DINE** effects in canary tenant; document remediation identity requirements in pattern README.
- **Exemptions:** separate Bicep module or JSON; include `expiresOn`, `metadata.assignedBy`, ticket/ADR reference.

Reference: [Bicep deploy policy assignments](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/governance/policy/how-to/policy-definition-structure) · [Deploy best practices](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-resource-manager/bicep/deploy-best-practices)

## Deployment stacks (optional)

- Use **deployment stacks** for lifecycle management when pattern owns a bounded RG and delete-resources-on-stack-delete is understood.
- Document stack action (add/modify/delete) in pipeline; not a substitute for what-if on production.

Reference: [Deployment stacks](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-resource-manager/bicep/deployment-stacks)

## Testing Bicep modules

| Check | Command / tool |
| --- | --- |
| Compile | `az bicep build --file main.bicep` |
| Lint | Bicep linter via VS Code / CI |
| Policy | PSRule for Azure (`Az.Resources`, `Azure.*` rules) |
| Preview | `az deployment group what-if` (production gate) |
| Contract | Assert required `outputs` consumed by parent module in CI script |

## Versioning & release

- **Semantic versioning** in `metadata module.version`; increment on breaking param/output changes.
- **Breaking change:** major bump + migration note in module README + orchestration `release/*` branch.
- Pin consumer `module` refs to registry **tag** or commit hash, not floating `main` in production configuration repos.